                            <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Limestone powder primarily consists of calcium carbonate (CaCO3). It may also contain small amounts of other minerals, depending on the composition of the original limestone rock. The presence of impurities can result in variations in color and characteristics of the powder.</p>
